# shellcheck shell=bash
# scripts/android/versions-blockchain.env -- pins of the blockchain node library
# (liblogos_blockchain.so, scripts/android/build-blockchain.sh) and of the blockchain_module
# plugin's native dependency libfyaml (scripts/android/build-libfyaml.sh).
#
# Sourced by those two scripts after scripts/android/env.sh (plain KEY=VALUE, bash syntax).
# Kept apart from versions.env so the runtime pins and the blockchain pins can move
# independently. Changing a pin changes the matching step's stamp key, so the next run
# redoes that step.
#
# Origin of the recipe: docs/research/exp-bc-android-build.md (experiment bc-android-build).

# --- Node revision --------------------------------------------------------------------
# logos-blockchain-module 4b07e58 (flake.lock) pins logos-blockchain 35a4a666 (master,
# 2026-09-22). Tag 0.3.0-rc.4 (39916dc8, 2026-09-23) is exactly that pin + 3 commits:
#   1a7768c Update inscribe                     deployment/ceremony/genesis/devnet/inscribe.yaml
#   3fd48e1 genesis ceremony for devnet 0.3.0-rc.4  nodes/node/binary/src/config/deployment/settings.yaml
#   39916dc Update cargo files                  Cargo.toml (reformat + workspace version
#                                               0.0.0 -> 0.3.0-rc.4), Cargo.lock (same bump)
# Verified from source (.work/scripts/m5lib-noderev.sh, build/logs/m5lib-noderev.log):
# merge-base(pin, rc.4) = pin; rc.4..pin is empty; `git diff 35a4a666 0.3.0-rc.4 -- c-bindings/`
# is EMPTY (0 lines). The C header is not committed: c-bindings/build.rs runs cbindgen on
# c-bindings/src only (cbindgen.toml: language C, no_includes, no parse_deps), so identical
# c-bindings sources give an identical logos_blockchain.h. build-blockchain.sh re-checks this
# on every build against LOGOS_BLOCKCHAIN_HEADER_SHA256 below (the header generated at
# 35a4a666 by the experiment).
# The lbc circuit crates (v0.5.7), rust-rapidsnark (e91187f8) and the toolchain (1.98.1) are
# the same at both revisions.
#
# Decision: build tag 0.3.0-rc.4. Its compiled-in deployment (settings.yaml) is the devnet
# 0.3.0-rc.4 genesis, so the module's start(cfg, "") joins devnet with no deployment file.
# (At 35a4a666 the compiled-in deployment is the placeholder chain 'standalone-local'; a pin
# build would need config/blockchain/deployment-devnet-0.3.0-rc.4.yaml passed to start().)
# Caveat: devnet protocol names are versioned per RC; the next devnet RC strands this build.
LOGOS_BLOCKCHAIN_REV=39916dc8c76c09afc5ea36bfcda138544cbf1553      # tag 0.3.0-rc.4
LOGOS_BLOCKCHAIN_VERSION=0.3.0-rc.4
LOGOS_BLOCKCHAIN_MODULE_PIN=35a4a666e22a51eb98fe8a050854e57fe3420899 # what module 4b07e58 locks (reference)
# sha256 of the cbindgen header (54 extern "C" functions) at 35a4a666 == expected at rc.4.
LOGOS_BLOCKCHAIN_HEADER_SHA256=b76d781aa9fe18b7aae5077a02f8b6e18c02f7c80f75fcefd6238fb66eca461e
RUST_TOOLCHAIN=1.98.1               # logos-blockchain rust-toolchain.toml (rustup honours it)

# --- Bedrock circuits (logos-blockchain-circuits) ---------------------------------------
# Version = the lbc-* tag in the node rev's Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock:
#   git+https://github.com/logos-blockchain/logos-blockchain-circuits.git?tag=v0.5.7#ebf7ddf5...
# (same in flake.nix: github:logos-blockchain/logos-blockchain-circuits/v0.5.7).
# build-blockchain.sh re-derives it from the checked-out Cargo.lock and fails on a mismatch.
LBC_VERSION=0.5.7
LBC_REV=ebf7ddf5b5b625ef4ea7c803171c670beebd05ef                    # tag v0.5.7
# Release bundle whose proving keys / verification keys / witness .dat files are embedded
# (include_bytes!) into the node library. The zkeys come from a per-release trusted-setup
# contribution (random), so they are NEVER regenerated: the Android LBC_ROOT_DIR takes them
# unchanged from this bundle. The data files are architecture-independent; the linux-x86_64
# bundle is used for every ABI. sha256 = hex of the SRI in the circuits repo's
# circuits-nix-hashes.json ("0.5.7"."x86_64-linux" = sha256-kqDGrYENSGYxUYt7myR6K2b2avb4+N3OOBrLvf7cD38=),
# which build-blockchain.sh cross-checks as well.
LBC_BUNDLE=logos-blockchain-circuits-v0.5.7-linux-x86_64
LBC_BUNDLE_URL=https://github.com/logos-blockchain/logos-blockchain-circuits/releases/download/v0.5.7/logos-blockchain-circuits-v0.5.7-linux-x86_64.tar.gz
LBC_BUNDLE_SHA256=92a0c6ad810d486631518b7b9b247a2b66f66af6f8f8ddce381acbbdfedc0f7f
LBC_BUNDLE_SRI=sha256-kqDGrYENSGYxUYt7myR6K2b2avb4+N3OOBrLvf7cD38=
# circom: the version the circuits CI pins (ci.yml CIRCOM_TAG v2.2.2; nixpkgs has 2.2.3).
CIRCOM_VERSION=2.2.2
CIRCOM_REV=e410b0d5cd2948a15931df0bc50d79ce56fa8c32                 # tag v2.2.2
# GMP: what rapidsnark's build_gmp.sh (circuits submodule) builds; it is run unmodified.
GMP_VERSION=6.2.1
GMP_URL=https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gmp/gmp-6.2.1.tar.xz
GMP_URL_ALT=https://gmplib.org/download/gmp/gmp-6.2.1.tar.xz
GMP_SHA256=fd4829912cddd12f84181c3451cc752be224643e87fac497b69edddadc49b4f2

# --- rapidsnark (prover) ----------------------------------------------------------------
# iden3 v0.0.8 Android prebuilts: the assets rust-rapidsnark e91187f8's download_rapidsnark.sh
# maps Android targets to, same version as the desktop Nix rapidsnark. PIC, libc++ (__ndk1).
RAPIDSNARK_VERSION=0.0.8
RAPIDSNARK_URL_BASE=https://github.com/iden3/rapidsnark/releases/download/v0.0.8
RAPIDSNARK_SHA256_x86_64=966d0e572963af1ff35faa56a5a16754a67000308d0cd89ed6c4d60a3080a2e0
RAPIDSNARK_SHA256_arm64=2e306704fe1b900261006ec41a7bef92bb3f94839c9989eff5058b133f5dc642

# --- libfyaml (blockchain_module plugin dependency) -------------------------------------
# The desktop module (metadata.json nix.runtime "libfyaml", CMake LINK_LIBRARIES fyaml)
# links nixpkgs 25.11's libfyaml 0.9 as a SHARED library (the .lgx ships libfyaml.so.0;
# /nix/store/*-libfyaml-0.9, configureFlags --disable-network, autotools). Android: the same
# 0.9 sources from the release tarball (pre-generated configure; the git archive's
# CMakeLists.txt is stale, project VERSION 0.7.2), shared, with the unversioned SONAME
# libfyaml.so (an APK cannot carry libfyaml.so.0).
LIBFYAML_VERSION=0.9
LIBFYAML_URL=https://github.com/pantoniou/libfyaml/releases/download/v0.9/libfyaml-0.9.tar.gz
LIBFYAML_SHA256=7731edc5dfcc345d5c5c9f6ce597133991a689dabede393cd77bae89b327cd6d
